{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2CO",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I determined this with myself, that I would not come again to you in heaviness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if I make you sorry, who is he then that maketh me glad, but the same who is made sorry by me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I wrote this same to you, lest, coming I should have sorrow from them by whom I ought to rejoice; having confidence in you all, that my joy is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the joy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of you all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For out of much affliction and anguish of heart I wrote to you with many tears; not that ye should be grieved, but that ye might know the love which I have more abundantly to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if any hath caused grief, he hath not grieved me, but in part: that I may not overcharge you all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sufficient to such a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this punishment, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was inflicted",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by many.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that on the other hand, ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ought",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rather to forgive ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and comfort ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", lest perhaps such one should be swallowed up with excessive sorrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I beseech you that ye would confirm ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love towards him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For to this end also I wrote, that I might know the proof of you, whether ye are obedient in all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom ye forgive any thing, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "forgive",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also: for if I forgave any thing, to whom I forgave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", for your sakes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I forgave it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", in the person of Christ;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest Satan should get an advantage of us: for we are not ignorant of his devices.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Furthermore, when I came to Troas to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "preach",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gospel of Christ, and a door was opened to me by the Lord,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I had no rest in my spirit, because I found not Titus my brother; but taking my leave of them, I went from thence into Macedonia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now thanks ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to God, who always causeth us to triumph in Christ, and maketh manifest the savor of his knowledge by us in every place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are to God a sweet savor of Christ, in them that are saved, and in them that perish:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "we are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the savor of death to death; and to the other the savor of life to life. And who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sufficient for these things?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are not as many, who corrupt the word of God: but as from sincerity, but as from God, in the sight of God we speak in Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
